## 5. Hardware — Pin Assignments (from `iot_old.md`)

| Component | ESP32 Pin | Protection Needed |
|-----------|-----------|-------------------|
| D2 Onboard LED | GPIO 2 | None (built-in) |
| Room 1 LED | GPIO 16 | **220Ω resistor** |
| Room 2 LED | GPIO 17 | **220Ω resistor** |
| Room 3 LED | GPIO 18 | **220Ω resistor** |
| Room 4 LED | GPIO 19 | **220Ω resistor** |
| HC-SR04 TRIG | GPIO 26 | None (3.3V ok) |
| HC-SR04 ECHO | GPIO 27 | **1kΩ + 2kΩ voltage divider** (5V → 3.3V) |
| HC-SR04 VCC | 5V pin | Not 3.3V! |
| SG90 Signal | GPIO 25 | None |
| SG90 VCC | 5V pin | **100µF cap to GND** |
| Active Buzzer (+) | GPIO 26 (old plan) / GPIO 23 | 100Ω optional |
| Flame Sensor (KY-026) D0 | GPIO 34 | None (input-only pin) |
| IR Sensor (FC-51) OUT | GPIO 35 | None (input-only pin) |

> [!WARNING]
> In the ChatGPT-revised ESP32 main.py (the serial version), **BUZZER was moved to GPIO 26** and **TRIG was moved to GPIO 5**. The original plan had BUZZER on GPIO 23 and TRIG on GPIO 26. This is a conflict if both are wired. Need to confirm final pin assignments before wiring.

> [!CAUTION]
> HC-SR04 ECHO outputs **5V** — connecting directly to ESP32 GPIO **WILL damage it**. The 1kΩ/2kΩ voltage divider is **mandatory**.

